# How to cite gemot. GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository" (APA and BibTeX).
# Bump `version` and `date-released` with `[project] version` in pyproject.toml at each release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gemot, please cite the preprint that describes it (preferred-citation)."
type: software
title: "gemot: an agent harness for building mechanistic models through PEtab MCP"
abstract: >-
  gemot is the agent harness built around the PEtab MCP server, which holds one PEtab v2
  parameter-estimation problem and lets an LLM agent change the model only through one
  constrained tool, with every change fitted, scored, versioned and justified. gemot runs a
  panel of agent specialists on that server, then a judge that scores the best version against
  a true or published reference, or by an absolute goodness-of-fit test, with the trace and
  version history kept for review.
authors:
  - name-particle: "de"
    family-names: "Pomereu"
    given-names: "Theodore"
  - family-names: "Snelling"
    given-names: "Branwen"
  - family-names: "Fröhlich"
    given-names: "Fabian"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/frohlich-lab/gemot"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/gemot/"
url: "https://github.com/frohlich-lab/gemot"
keywords:
  - PEtab
  - Model Context Protocol
  - LLM agents
  - systems biology
  - mechanistic modelling
  - parameter estimation
